The question asks whether an interface in PHP can declare constants.

In PHP, interfaces can indeed declare constants. Interface constants are always public and readonly by nature (they can't be changed). This is a valid PHP feature.

Example:
```php
interface MyInterface {
    const FOO = "bar";
}
```

So the answer is "yes".

